# C++20 build standard

All C++ in this repository **must be compiled with C++20**. The local
Accellera SystemC and CCI installs are built with C++20, and SystemC's ABI is
keyed per language standard (`sc_api_version_*_cxx202002L`). Compiling consumers
with any other standard breaks linking with an undefined `sc_api_version_*`
symbol.

## Reference toolchain (C++20)

- SystemC: `/Users/pdroy/local/systemc-3.0.2-cxx20`
- CCI:     `/Users/pdroy/local/cci-cxx20`

## When configuring CMake / running tests

Force C++20 and point at the C++20 installs:

```bash
SYSTEMC_HOME=/Users/pdroy/local/systemc-3.0.2-cxx20 \
CCI_HOME=/Users/pdroy/local/cci-cxx20 \
cmake -S . -B build -DSMC_CXX_STANDARD=20 -DCCI_HOME=/Users/pdroy/local/cci-cxx20
```

The `smc/cmake/SmcSystemCStd.cmake` helper auto-detects the standard from the
linked SystemC, so pointing at the C++20 install already yields C++20; pass
`-DSMC_CXX_STANDARD=20` to be explicit. Never hard-code a different standard.

## When writing CMakeLists.txt

```cmake
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
set(CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS OFF)
```

Prefer including `SmcSystemCStd` and calling `smc_detect_systemc_cxx_std()`
(which resolves to C++20 against this toolchain) over hard-coding the value.

## Source code

Write portable C++ that is clean under C++20 (also C++17/23). Do not use
constructs removed/deprecated by C++20 (e.g. `std::result_of`, `std::is_pod`,
throwing `std::allocator`).
